From 313cc9f76c950fe08c081274be91c9409e4e2bdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jesse <jesse@jjo.ninja>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 20:48:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] linux-postmarketos-qcom-sc7180: add camera support for
 google-trogdor wormdingler

Add the SC7180 camera subsystem (CAMSS), the CCI camera I2C controller
and the two MIPI cameras of the Lenovo IdeaPad Duet 3 (wormdingler):
OV5675 (front) and OV8856 (rear, with DW9714 VCM). Enable the sensor and
VCM drivers as modules.

Patches 0006-0022 are the series being sent upstream ("media: qcom:
camss: Add SC7180 support and the Lenovo IdeaPad Duet 3 cameras", v3 of
George Chan's 2024 series with fixes), 0023-0028 are i2c-qcom-cci
runtime PM fixes already in mainline 6.19 that avoid a WARN on resume.

Tested on wormdingler: both cameras stream at 30 fps with libcamera
(simple pipeline + software ISP), Plasma Camera works, PipeWire lists
both cameras, suspend/resume is clean.
